      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the weight of one of the bowling balls, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the weight of one canoe.\n2. Use the weight of one canoe to find the weight of one bowling ball.\n\nFirst, we know that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds. Therefore, the weight of one canoe is:\n\\[\n\\text{Weight of one canoe} = \\frac{56 \\text{ pounds}}{2} = 28 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that seven identical bowling balls weigh the same as three identical canoes. Since we have already found that one canoe weighs 28 pounds, three canoes weigh:\n\\[\n\\text{Weight of three canoes} = 3 \\times 28 \\text{ pounds} = 84 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nSince seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes, the weight of seven bowling balls is also 84 pounds. Therefore, the weight of one bowling ball is:\n\\[\n\\text{Weight of one bowling ball} = \\frac{84 \\text{ pounds}}{7} = 12 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nThus, the weight of one bowling ball is \\boxed{12}.",
